  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "FPGA \"Pin\" numbers matched to header rows in the same row/column order as the label grids (confirmed for PMOD2 by the cross-shaped P2/Pin legend). Snap-off PMOD module header uses the P2 labels from the mirrored right-hand grid; its LED/button legend (LED1-LED5, Button 1-3) is a separate table and not merged into pins. CRESET 2-pin jumper has no per-pin labels and is not transcribed. Labels printed on two lines (e.g. \"P1 / A1\") joined with a space. Two-name flash boxes (e.g. \"MOSI / IO0\"): top line used as label, second line as function. FLASH pin 1 silkscreen shows CS with an overbar."
